WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.860
One fair wage!

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.620
One fair wage!

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.920
Restaurant workers are being ripped off,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.960
say these protesters because they aren't

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.980
guaranteed minimum wage.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.440
In 43 states, employers are allowed to pay

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.120
tipped workers less,

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.860
some as little as $2.13 an hour.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.360
Celebrities plus union protests convinced voters and

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.399
politicians in several states

00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:29.080
that the government must insist on

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.020
a higher minimum for tipped workers.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.180
This would be more fair for

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.780
all workers,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.560
specifically for minorities and women.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.560
They always say that it's to

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.560
"help minorities and women."

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.400
How is everything today?

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.700
But waitress Alcieli Felipe is a minority

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.820
and a woman.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.740
Coffee?

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.600
She says,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.640
don't change the rules on tips.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.538
We have spaghetti and meatballs.

00:00:54.538 --> 00:00:55.320
Thanks to tips,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.360
Alcieli makes much more than minimum wage.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.440
It's free refills, you're good.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.040
I'll make $25 dollars an hour.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.360
By the end of the year,

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.080
I made around $48 to $50 thousand dollars.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.300
I'll take this for you.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.994
If you raise the minimum wage,

00:01:08.994 --> 00:01:10.858
it will be harder for restaurants

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.480
to keep the same amount of employees.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:17.060
No, no say the so-called public interest lawyers.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.020
We have to have a law.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.220
The problem with tips is that they're very inconsistent.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.080
Law professor Nicole Hallett leads social justice

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:24.980
protests,

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.580
this one demanding that

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.180
tipped workers be paid that higher minimum wage.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.580
Require restaurant owners

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.600
to pay the same hourly wage

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.280
that all other employers have to pay.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.580
Save our jobs!

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.600
But many restaurant workers say

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.020
don't raise the minimum,

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.560
a higher minimum

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.900
threatens our jobs.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.694
The cost of having a restaurant

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.480
is not cheap.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.260
For my boss to pay all her employees,

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:51.680
she would have to cut employees;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.700
the busboy will be cut.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.220
Hallett is unconvinced.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.680
I simply don't believe that increasing the minimum wage

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.600
for tipped workers will lead in a reduction

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.680
in the restaurant workforce.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.040
Studies have shown that

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.720
restaurants have been able to bear those costs.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.540
Someone has to clear the plates.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.560
But in New York after the last minimum wage increase,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.220
270 restaurants closed.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.555
But restaurants always close.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.320
The industry is doing just fine.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.940
Restaurants don't always close.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.460
Michael Saltsman works for an employer group that

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.380
fights minimum wage increases.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.840
Yeah, there's turnover in the industry.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:24.660
But what we're doing now

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.060
is we're taking an industry

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.900
where there's low profit margins

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.000
we're dramatically increasing labor costs,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.660
and we're jacking up restaurant closures.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.780
If in the Bay Area,

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.180
you've got a 14% increase in restaurant closures

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.360
for each dollar increase in the minimum wage,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.680
something's not right.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:39.640
That isn't right,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.020
but the media is all about workers

00:02:42.023 --> 00:02:43.400
who are unhappy.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.040
And go home with no money.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.580
I don't think that it's fair for a worker to

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.080
struggle to pay rent, to struggle to meet groceries.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.020
One study found that 46 percent

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.940
of tipped workers nationwide

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.680
rely on public benefits.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.760
Like food stamps.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.660
But even Hallett admits many are only eligible because

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.020
a lot of people don't report tipped income.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.080
Many restaurants and restaurant workers

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.220
often don't report 100% of their income.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.040
So the fact they're getting benefits

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.920
doesn't mean anything,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.440
it just means that they're cheating the taxpayer.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.760
Alcieli says she doesn't cheat

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.440
but many other people do.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:20.780
Lots of people make cash money, tip only.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.820
Tons of restaurants do that.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.020
Have a great day hon.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.820
Those who demand higher minimums also claim

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.260
eliminating tips will reduce sexual harassment,

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.700
another argument embraced by the media.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.700
90% of restaurant workers

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.540
report experiencing sexual behavior

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:39.960
that is scary or unwanted.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.580
90%?

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.340
90%.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.100
Tipping is pretty dependent on her willingness

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.260
to touch or be touched.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.000
This'll reduce sexual harassment.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Sexual harassment has nothing to do

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.320
with the state's tipping system,

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.660
and it's not me saying that,

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.360
it's the federal government saying that.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.900
A study using federal data

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.500
did find that states that raised the minimum

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.600
actually had

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:02.220
Increases in sexual harassment.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.920
The states that did what you want, there are more

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.020
charges of sexual harassment.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:11.040
Sexual harassment is a very complicated problem

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.800
and no single policy is going to

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.120
eliminate that problem.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.520
Ok, so raising the minimum

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.100
probably won't affect sexual harassment,

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.480
but it will force some restaurants to fire workers

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.100
and force some to close.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.580
Since prices will be higher, tips will go down.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.820
This is supposed to be good for restaurant workers?

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.640
Save our jobs!

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.260
No wonder so many opposed

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.220
what the activists demand.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.060
Just keep as it is,

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.480
we are fine.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.640
Who are those people,

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.980
have they worked in a restaurant industry?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.140
She hasn't

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.180
and all this makes me ask,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.000
why should there be any minimum?

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.380
Why can't the employer and the employee

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.540
make whatever deal they want?

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.960
Well, that policy has been rejected.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.200
It's

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.020
something that has been rejected

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.740
for the last hundred years and

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.660
we're not in that world right now.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.900
We sure aren't.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.680
We're in a world where activists and government

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.200
protect workers,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.860
even when they don't want

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:13.100
that protection.

